<Docs
    title="Docs"
    description="How to get a Tern node running and use it: a board, the firmware, an app, and your first contact."
>
    <h1>Start here</h1>
    <p class="lede">
        Tern is a LoRa mesh: small radios that pass short messages to each other over kilometres, with no phone
        network or internet. You carry or place a <strong>node</strong>, a board running Tern's firmware, and
        use it from an <strong>app</strong> on your phone or computer.
    </p>

    <div class="note">
        <p>
            Tern is early. The firmware is an alpha, a later release may not talk to an earlier one, and nobody
            outside the project has yet reviewed its cryptography. It is for trying out, not for anything you depend
            on.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>In five steps</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>
            <strong>Get a board</strong>, the 863-928 MHz kind: any of those on <a href="/docs/hardware">Hardware</a>.
            The Heltec WiFi LoRa 32 V3 is the one checked on hardware so far; the others are built and waiting to be
            tried.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Fit its antenna</strong> before you power it. A board sends as soon as it starts, and a radio
            sending with no antenna can damage itself.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Flash it</strong> from <a href="/flash">the flash page</a>, in Chrome or Edge on a computer, over
            USB. Choose the region you are in.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Get an app</strong>: <a href="/apps">Android, iPhone, iPad, Mac</a>, or <a href="/app">the
            browser</a>. Connect to the node over Bluetooth and type the passkey its screen shows.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Add someone.</strong> Scan the QR code on their node's screen or app, or open their node's link.
            Check the twelve-digit code with them, then write.
        </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
        With two boards of your own you can try all of it on a desk: drive one from a phone and the other from
        the browser app, add each as the other's contact, and write. <a href="/docs/guide">Using Tern</a> goes through each step.
    </p>

